Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos8895: allow more concurrent DECON buffers

The 1440x2960 linear 32-bit scanout needs about 16.3 MiB per buffer
before alignment. On the running GNOME Wayland handset the 96 MiB
DECON pool cannot allocate one additional panel-sized buffer.
Importing ordinary Panfrost shmem buffers into DECON is also rejected,
so the display needs room to retain the old scanout during replacement.

Use 160 MiB of reusable CMA for the display. Keep the original low
address window and alignment because DECON accepts only 32-bit DMA
addresses. Leave the global CMA size and other consumers alone.

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos8895-dream2lteks.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos8895-dream2lteks.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos8895-dream2lteks.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos8895-dream2lteks.dts
@@ -49,7 +49,7 @@
 		g955n_decon_pool: decon-dma-pool {
 			compatible = "shared-dma-pool";
 			reusable;
-			size = <0x06000000>;
+			size = <0x0a000000>;
 			alignment = <0 0x00400000>;
 			alloc-ranges = <0 0x80000000 0x3c800000>;
 		};
